schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: Understanding Gas Fees in Cryptocurrency
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: concept
  summary: >-
    A quick, plain-language explainer of blockchain gas fees: what gas is and
    why it exists (pay validators, prevent spam, allocate block space), the
    EIP-1559 base-fee + tip fee model (base fee auto-adjusts with demand and
    is burned; priority fee/tip jumps the queue), typical gas costs by
    transaction type, what drives fees up or down (network demand, time of
    day, transaction complexity), and five ways to save (time transactions,
    avoid volatility spikes, use fee estimators, use Layer 2, set max fees).
  audience: newcomers doing their first crypto transactions
  known_tensions: []
  related_concepts:
    - gas-fee-eip-1559-base-fee-plus-tip-model
  related_resources:
    - arbitrum
    - optimism
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/gas-fees.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted

